WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:01.501
- I'm Rob Lowe.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.044
- And I'm John Owen Lowe.

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:04.462
- And we're going to answer some questions

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:06.715
from inside this cookie jar.

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:09.467
(dramatic music)

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.016
- Let's pick one.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:18.977
- Johnny, your oldest Instagram post

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:21.146
is a picture from an Elton John show.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.856
Kinda looks like he's yelling at you

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.524
for taking the picture though.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.109
(screaming)

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:26.943
What's something

00:00:26.943 --> 00:00:30.613
in your life you wish you
had photographic evidence of?

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:33.283
- Good question.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:35.952
When I beat you for the
first time in tennis

00:00:35.952 --> 00:00:37.120
and you almost cried.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.538
- I don't think that's true.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.956
- That's why I need evidence.

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:43.334
- I'm now going to lift the head.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:46.129
- Okay.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.341
John Owen, sometimes you go by Johnny,

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:52.135
but sometimes you've gone by John.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:54.971
This show is now called
Bro'in with John Owen.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.182
What?

00:00:57.182 --> 00:01:02.187
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:06.983
Hi, my name is say your name,

00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:08.568
welcome to Bro'in with John Owen.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.986
Have you ever wondered how many Johns

00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:12.906
can John Owen Lowe can shout
out in under 30 seconds?

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.907
Let's find out.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.742
Ready, set, go.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.412
John Stamos, Elton John, John Legend.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.914
John Lennon.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.332
John Wayne Gacy.

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.543
Ah, John.

00:01:25.543 --> 00:01:26.377
- Jacob Jingleheimer Schmidt.

00:01:26.377 --> 00:01:28.004
- Jacob Jingleheimer Schmidt.

00:01:28.004 --> 00:01:30.381
John Florence. He's a surfer.

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:31.257
John.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.842
- Kennedy.
- Kennedy.

00:01:32.842 --> 00:01:35.053
John Paul Gaultier,

00:01:35.053 --> 00:01:36.679
that's a Jean, I think, dammit!

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.891
God!

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:45.522
(upbeat suspenseful music)

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:48.733
- Rob, you were one of the
stars of the 1983 classic

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.735
"The Outsiders," where
you played a character

00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:51.820
named Soda Pop.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.489
To officially end this age old debate,

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.033
should sugary carbonated drinks

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.744
be referred to as soda or pop?

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:01.996
Well, you know the answer to
that depends on where you live.

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.748
It's a geographical question.

00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:07.127
Pop is a Midwestern, now I'm from Ohio,

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.128
we call them pop.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:11.005
Soda is everywhere but the Midwest.

00:02:11.005 --> 00:02:12.674
(horse neighing)

00:02:12.674 --> 00:02:16.553
So the answer is depends
on where you live.

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:18.346
(ice clinking)

00:02:18.346 --> 00:02:19.514
- Whatever.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:20.598
- And now, once again,

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:22.517
for the ceremonial lifting of the head.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:25.353
- Rob, you were a member

00:02:25.353 --> 00:02:27.397
of the infamous Brat Pack back in the day.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.566
Bratwurst is a type of German sausage.

00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.693
How would you rate your
bratwurst grilling skills?

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:34.195
Das ist gut or are you ze worst?

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:36.156
- Well you know, I think
that it's very good.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.366
You have the mustard and then
you course you have the kraut

00:02:38.366 --> 00:02:40.577
and then you know, you put
it in some kind of a bread

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:42.829
and you feed it to a mini horse.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.289
- It's good.

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:45.456
Get in there.

00:02:45.456 --> 00:02:46.291
Go quick.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.002
- Lowe's.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:49.961
- That's us.

00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:52.672
- This ain't your first rodeo
sharing the screen together.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.799
In fact, you previously had a show called

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:57.552
"The Lowe Files" where
you investigated UFOs.

00:02:57.552 --> 00:03:00.388
Among other things, okay, not just UFOs.

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:04.726
On a scale of comet bacteria
to aliens built the pyramids,

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:05.894
and I think they might have,

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:07.770
where do your beliefs land now?

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.522
Is the truth out there?

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.107
Well, I just returned from Egypt

00:03:11.107 --> 00:03:12.775
to find these things out myself

00:03:12.775 --> 00:03:14.402
and I was a big believer

00:03:14.402 --> 00:03:16.112
that maybe the aliens built the pyramids.

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:17.780
But after having just been there,

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.157
I think that the pyramids

00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:22.994
might just have been built by Egyptians.

00:03:22.994 --> 00:03:24.287
- Okay.
- Boring.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:26.164
- Yeah. It's all nonsense.

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:27.040
- All nonsense?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.958
- Yeah. Well, I mean maybe aliens.

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.793
- But you were the resident cynic always.

00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:32.712
- Yeah, that's the rational take.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:33.963
- But what about the disclosure?

00:03:33.963 --> 00:03:36.549
All the UAPs, as they call 'em.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.508
- The what?

00:03:37.508 --> 00:03:38.885
- He doesn't read the news.

00:03:40.011 --> 00:03:41.262
I was supposed to remove the head.

00:03:41.262 --> 00:03:43.181
- No. Okay. Yeah, whatever you'll be okay.

00:03:44.182 --> 00:03:46.559
Ben? Is there a Ben?

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:50.355
I don't know who Ben is.

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:51.940
- This is really good.
- Let's try and figure out

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.067
- Let's try to get to the Ben.
- Who this Ben is.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.236
- Is it Ben Affleck?

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.195
Is it Uncle Ben?
- If he's Ben Affleck,

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:58.029
that's pretty cool.

00:03:58.029 --> 00:03:58.863
- Is it Uncle Ben?
- I know.

00:03:58.863 --> 00:03:59.822
- Stove Top stuffing?

00:03:59.822 --> 00:04:01.783
- There's a Ben on "Shadow and Bone."

00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:02.617
- Ooh.

00:04:03.826 --> 00:04:05.453
This whole Ben thing that's going on.

00:04:05.453 --> 00:04:07.121
- I'm not liking where this is going.

00:04:07.121 --> 00:04:08.164
- Me neither.
- Ben.

00:04:08.164 --> 00:04:10.750
The point is, Ben, get
out of our interview.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.584
- Yeah.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.418
- This is about us.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.461
- This is my interview for my show.

00:04:13.461 --> 00:04:14.379
- It's our show.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.006
(bleep) Ben.

00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:21.135
- Rob, in your new show "Unstable,"

00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:23.137
you play a character named Ellis Dragon.

00:04:23.137 --> 00:04:25.390
If you rearrange the
letters in Ellis Dragon

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.684
you get Ireland slog.

00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:30.520
The direct slog from Los Angeles

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.564
to Dublin takes 10 hours, shite.

00:04:33.564 --> 00:04:35.858
How are you getting through that flight?

00:04:35.858 --> 00:04:37.026
On a flight of that length,

00:04:37.026 --> 00:04:38.653
it's almost the perfect amount of time

00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:41.322
to watch all of season one of "Unstable."

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.075
- Okay, well that's enough of that.

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:46.286
Thank you so much for watching and...

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:49.664
- And check out "Unstable" season one.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.791
Squeezed.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:52.625
- Don't you know when it comes out?

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:55.420
- "Unstable" season one now
streaming only on Netflix.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.254
- What day?

00:04:56.254 --> 00:04:57.088
March 30th.

00:04:57.088 --> 00:04:58.131
- I just says now streaming.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.132
It doesn't say the date.

